  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **banter - inviting Marco**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **The Swamp**: rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Revolution (Beatles)**: back after 25 archived shows (375 days); rare: 14 archived performances [5]\n- **The Ocean**: back after 25 archived shows (375 days) [5]\n- **banter - inviting Shady Horns and David Hidalgo**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Who Knows What Tomorrow May Bring?**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Dream In Blue**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Chains Of Love**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 19 songs; 152 min [1]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21.flac16**: audience recording; 19 songs; 152 min [2]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21-cmc65omnimix.flac16**: audience recording; 19 songs; 152 min [4]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21-cmc65omnimix.flac24**: audience recording; 19 songs; 152 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Show was Night 5 of Bowlive IV, with The London Souls opening [1]\n- Shady Horns joined: Ryan Zoidis, James Casey and Eric Bloom, all adding percussion alongside their horns [1]\n- Marco Benevento sat in on Fender Rhodes; David Hidalgo played guitar; the whole London Souls band also joined [1]\n- Part of Bowlive IV, Night 5, opened by The London Souls [2]\n- Guests included Shady Horns, Marco Benevento on Rhodes, David Hidalgo on guitar, and the full London Souls band [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [1]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]. Also: A four-microphone on-stage mix also exists, adding a split pair of Schoeps mk5 omnis placed ten feet apart [2]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21-cmc65omnimix.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/4-Mic On Stage Mix [4]. Also: Main pair: Schoeps mk21 cardioids, NOS, on stage, through KC-5 capsules, Sonosax preamp, into Sound Devices 744T at 24/96; Second source: Schoeps cmc65 omnis split ten feet, via Lunatec ACM V3 into the 744T; mixed in Vegas Pro; Mix was normalized and faded in SoundForge, resampled to 44.1 kHz with iZotope, dithered to 16 bit, then encoded to FLAC [4]\n- **soulive2013-03-13.mk21-cmc65omnimix.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/4-Mic On Stage Mix [3]",
